# Units are enabled and started in this order by `make services-check`
# (bootstrap) and driven by services-start / services-stop / restart.
# check-x-server runs FIRST and exports DISPLAY to the user manager
# environment (on-deploy detect-server --persist-to-systemd); every WM
# unit is After=/Requires= it and carries no hardcoded display.
# xvfb x11vnc novnc form the headless/VNC stack (commented out here;
# x11vnc falls back to the localhost:0.0 convention when check-x-server
# is not enabled). Providers: check-x-server AND xvfb both declare
# Alias=x-server.service — enable exactly ONE, the enabled one claims
# the alias (herbst claims Alias=x-window-manager.service).
#xvfb x11vnc herbst novnc dunst compton
check-x-server herbst dunst compton hc_send-error-daemon
